  "summary": [
    "Batch A, family A6 (ordinary graph complement). Five relation/constructor pairs (X3, chromatic XE2, X56, extremal XE1, X29), all `(x != y) && ~~ (x -- y)` with an SGraph built from their own symmetry and irreflexivity proofs, now unfold to upstream `compl_rel` and `compl`. The relations agree by conversion; the graphs are related by the identity isomorphism (`compl_eq_diso`), not by equality of the opaque proof fields, which are frozen verbatim as scaffolding. Sixteen statements are affected (X3, chromatic XE2, X56, X29, eight extremal XE1 and four extremal XE2 Ramsey rows) through four intermediate predicates (`x3_complement_image` and the XE1 Ramsey, Ramsey-number and diagonal chain). Transports move along the identity isomorphism: X3 keeps the same class witness, X56's complement is the forbidden pattern of `induced_free`, X29's is the host of an induced cycle, the Ramsey chain's is the host of an ordinary subgraph, and the choice number of X3/XE2 complements converts.",
    "",
    "History: A1's X56 snapshot and A5's Ramsey chain (and B4's erdos_567 snapshot) still call live complement names and are documented below. X56Original combines A1's frozen induced-free helper with the frozen complement; XE1Original and XE2Original combine A5's frozen subgraph helper with the frozen complement for all twelve Ramsey rows, and erdos_567 also with B4's frozen h5_graph. Other live helpers in these rows (for instance x4_edge_count) are not migrated, so no row is claimed to be a pre-M1 original. No statement text, doc block, manifest row, leg state or discrepancy changes."
  ],
